---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service" description="Terms of service and acceptable use guidelines for the QR Code Generator.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">Last Updated: August 2026</p>
      </div>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>
          You agree not to use the QR Code Generator for any unlawful activities, phishing, malware distribution, harassment, spam campaigns, or infringing intellectual property.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Prohibited Link Destinations</h2>
        <p>
          Dynamic QR codes pointing to dangerous protocols (including <code>javascript:</code>, <code>data:</code>, or <code>file:</code> URIs) or known malicious phishing domains will be immediately disabled by our automated moderation filters.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The service is provided "AS IS" without warranties of any kind. You are responsible for testing scannability and contrast on your target print medium before running large print production runs.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
